AI-Powered SQL Generation and Retrieval System
This project is part of a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline built using Python, LangChain, and SQLite. It translates natural language search requests (such as finding hotels with specific features and dates) into valid SQL queries by leveraging an LLM paired with the underlying database schema and sample data.

Features
Automated Schema Extraction: Connects to a SQLite database and extracts table definitions alongside representative sample rows to maximize LLM query accuracy.

Prompt-Driven SQL Generation: Uses custom PromptTemplate configurations to guide the LLM on syntax rules, security best practices, date references, and formatting requirements.

LangChain Expression Language (LCEL): Implements a clean, pipe-delimited (|) data pipeline connecting the prompt template directly to the chat model.

